  "body": "### What is the issue with the MIME Sniffing Standard?\r\n\r\nThe section \"Interpreting the resource metadata\" / \"To determine the supplied MIME type of a resource\" has the step: \"If supplied-type is not a [MIME type](https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#mime-type), the [supplied MIME type](https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#supplied-mime-type) is undefined.\"\r\n\r\nThe \"MIME type\" link doesn't define how to determine whether a string is or is not a MIME type.  Does it mean if the \"parsing a MIME type\" algorithm returns failure, or something else?",
